if TARGET_ONYX_RC2

config SYS_BOARD
	default "onyx-rc2"

config SYS_VENDOR
	default "rockchip"

config SYS_CONFIG_NAME
	default "onyx_rc2"

config RC2_RESET_METHOD
	string "Default reset method (core, fst or snd)"
	default "core"
	help
	  How the "reset" command (and anything else that asks the sysreset
	  uclass for a reset) resets the RK3026. The environment variable
	  rc2_reset overrides it at run time, so the device test can try
	  every method without a rebuild.

	  core: the stock 3.0 kernel's way, from IMEM: all PLLs to slow
	        mode, then SOFTRST_CON0 = 0x801cffff (MCORE, CORE0, CORE1,
	        L2C). The GPIO banks, the GRF, IMEM and the DDR controller
	        keep their state, so the ACT8931 power hold (GPIO1_A2) stays
	        up: on battery the book restarts (U-Boot "reset" with the
	        cable pulled: Linux back 9 s later, pstore kept; 2026-10-18).
	        The stock kernel's reboot from SD lands on the SD.
	  fst:  CRU_GLB_SRST_FST_VALUE = 0xfdb9 (first global reset). On the
	        book after a mainline "reboot" it ran ROM -> FlashData ->
	        stage2 from the SD again (2026-10-17). Resets the GPIO banks
	        (2026-10-18): on battery the power hold drops and the book
	        switches off. After it the host did not see U-Boot's ACM
	        port again.
	  snd:  CRU_GLB_SRST_SND_VALUE = 0xeca8 (second global reset; keeps
	        the GRF, resets the GPIO banks like fst: on battery the book
	        switches off, 2026-10-18).

	  Every method first cleans and disables the caches and clears the
	  IMEM remap. With the cable in all three bring the BootROM back to
	  the microSD card; on battery only core does (book rounds of
	  2026-10-17 and 2026-10-18).

endif
